{"reference":"Ezekiel 27","book":"Ezekiel","chapter":27,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A question about Tyre","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Ezekiel 27 is a lament over historical Tyre, portraying it as a splendid trading ship whose ruin is mourned. The related portrayals of Tyre and its rulers in Ezekiel 26-28 use siege, ship, lament, garden, precious-stone, and cherub imagery; this reading is disputed, but the chapters do not explicitly name Satan.","verse_refs":["Ezekiel 27:1-36"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ezekiel_027_81a070939401d2e4f0c2b11a"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}